## Context

Final prose quality pass on `slides/manuscript/main.md` once structure and
science are clean. Blocked by 0512 (structural numbering must be stable).

## What to do

**Contributions list (§1 end).**
Add a short bullet list naming the three contributions:
1. Benchmark gap — first sourced evaluation of AI agents on national
   power-plant inventory construction with per-cell provenance.
2. Per-row provenance × temporality scoring — four-dimension quality bar
   applied to LLM-generated tables.
3. Two-grain credibility/reliability scoring (run-level vs model-level,
   STANAG 2511 Admiralty analogy).

**GPT-5.5 principled refusals.**
Surface in §4 results and Discussion: GPT-5.5 declining to fabricate
primary-sourced citations is evidence about the epistemic standard being
tested. Currently buried in Annex B bold sentence.

**Annex A.**
Keep T1/T2 paragraphs (snapshot vs flow, as-of date). Cut the
Parmenides/Heraclitus → IFRS → IAM philosophy genealogy.

**Language fixes (representative list).**
- "random words generator somewhere in the cloud" → "plausible-text
  generator"
- "How well do the state of the art tools perform when it comes to
  producing research-quality statistical datasets?" → "How well do
  state-of-the-art tools perform at producing research-grade statistical
  datasets?"
- "FP … unrecognized plants" → "unmatched plants (extracted but not in
  the reference)" everywhere (Figures 2, 5, 7, body text)
- Em-dash pass: convert ~50% of em-dashes in long sentences to commas,
  colons, or sentence breaks.
- Figure 3 caption (~200 words): move methods to Annex B, keep only
  what the eye needs.
- British spelling consistent throughout (optimised, colour, Annex not
  Appendix).

